course: dictionary
lesson: 8370
title: Rouse: wake up or stir up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word rouse has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. «Next morning Toad slept very soundly, and no amount of shaking could rouse him.» Shaking a sleeper is a way of waking them, so here rouse means to wake someone up.
explain: Rouse can also mean to make someone feel a strong emotion, like excitement or anger, or to make them act. A leader can rouse a crowd with a speech. Then the word rousing describes something loud and exciting, like a rousing song or a rousing cheer.
explain: In Australia, people use an informal phrase, rouse on, which means to tell someone off. You will only meet this in Australian speech, so check the words around it. When you are unsure, try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: Rouse is a verb, and its forms are rouses, roused and rousing.
fact: «Rouse» means to wake someone up, as in «rouse from sleep».
fact: «Rouse» can also mean to make people excited, angry or ready to act, as in «rouse a crowd».
fact: «Rousing» means loud, exciting and stirring, as in «a rousing speech».
fact: In Australia, informal «rouse on» means to tell someone off.
exercise: «No amount of shaking could rouse him.» What does rouse mean here? | To cook a meal | *To wake someone up | To paint a wall
exercise: The leader's speech began to rouse the crowd. What does rouse mean here? | To leave the room quietly | To put people to sleep | *To make people excited or ready to act
exercise: The sergeant says, «Rouse thee, old loon.» What does rouse mean? | *To wake up | To go to bed early | To sit down quietly | To be quiet
test: «The rousing song made everyone clap and cheer.» What does rousing mean? | Sad and slow | *Loud and exciting | Quiet and sleepy
test: An Australian teacher says she will rouse on a pupil who was late. What does rouse on mean? | *To tell someone off | To wake someone up | To hug someone warmly
exam: Which phrase means to wake someone from sleep? | *rouse from sleep | rouse suspicion | rousing speech | rouse on
